sSold\":1,\"screenId\":\"164\",\"seatsRemaining\":56,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc3\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"275279\",\"time\":\"2025-03-06T19:40:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"164\",\"seatsRemaining\":57,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc3\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"277343\",\"time\":\"2025-03-07T17:15:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"164\",\"seatsRemaining\":57,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc3\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"21138\",\"name\":\"Bridget Jones Mad About The Boy\",\"showingStatus\":\"Now Playing\",\"urlSlug\":\"bridget-jones-mad-about-the-boy\",\"posterImage\":\"24cck0ctuguz7rr0y3y0u43cma3q\",\"bannerImage\":\"t9glsq2yodgbrhmdyjk82c3ga4le\",\"synopsis\":\"Two-time Academy Award® winner Renée Zellweger returns to the role that established a romantic-comedy heroine for the ages, a woman whose inimitable approach to life and love redefined an entire film genre.\\n\\nBridget Jones first blasted onto bookshelves in Helen Fielding’s literary phenomenon Bridget Jones’s Diary, which became a global bestseller and a blockbuster film. As a single career woman living in London, Bridget Jones not only introduced the world to her romantic adventures, but added “Singletons,” “Smug-Marrieds” and “f---wittage” into the global lexicon. Bridget’s ability to triumph despite adversity led her to finally marry top lawyer Mark Darcy and to become the mother of their baby boy. Happiness at last.\\n\\nBut in Bridget Jones: Mad About the Boy, Bridget is alone once again, widowed four years ago, when Mark was killed on a humanitarian mission in the Sudan. She’s now a single mother to 9-year-old Billy and 4-year-old Mabel, and is stuck in a state of emotional limbo, raising her children with help from her loyal friends and even her former lover, Daniel Cleaver (Hugh Grant).\\n\\nPressured by her Urban Family —Shazzer, Jude and Tom, her work colleague Miranda, her mother, and her gynecologist Dr. Rawlings (Oscar® winner Emma Thompson) — to forge a new path toward life and love, Bridget goes back to work and even tries out the dating apps, where she’s soon pursued by a dreamy and enthusiastic younger man (White Lotus’s Leo Woodall). Now juggling work, home and romance, Bridget grapples with the judgment of the perfect mums at school, worries about Billy as he struggles with the absence of his father, and engages in a series of awkward interactions with her son’s rational-to-a-fault science teacher (Oscar® nominee Chiwetel Ejiofor).\",\"starring\":\"Renée Zellweger, Chiwetel Ejiofor, Leo Woodall, Hugh Grant, Jim Broadbent, Gemma Jones, Colin Firth\",\"directedBy\":\"Michael Morris\",\"producedBy\":\"Eric Fellner, Tim Bevan, Jo Wallett\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":125,\"genre\":\"Comedy\",\"allGenres\":\"Comedy, Drama, Romance\",\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"fc5zbSCgudA\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-02-14\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-02-13\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":280.956,\"tmdbId\":\"1272149\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"415782\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Bridget Jones: Mad About The Boy (2D) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"101\",\"titleClassId\":\"75\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"262888\",\"time\":\"2025-02-13T14:15:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":42,\"screenId\":\"162\",\"seatsRemaining\":58,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"262887\",\"time\":\"2025-02-13T17:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":34,\"screenId\":\"162\",\"seatsRemaining\":66,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"262886\",\"time\":\"2025-02-13T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":68,\"screenId\":\"162\",\"seatsRemaining\":32,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"262889\",\"time\":\"2025-02-14T14:15:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":25,\"screenId\":\"162\",\"seatsRemaining\":75,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"reserved-seating sc1\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"262890\",\"time\":\"2025-02-14T17:0